request.description:
Open this WebSocket while logged in as the tutor. On connection, the backend replays up to 100 unread persisted notifications. Booking notifications use notification_type=SERVICE_BOOKED; approval notifications use SERVICE_APPROVED or SERVICE_REVISION_APPROVED. Students booked on an upcoming service receive SERVICE_UPDATED after an approved service update.

Expected notification frame:
{
  "event": "notification",
  "payload": {
    "id": "notification-uuid",
    "user_id": "recipient-user-uuid",
    "notification_type": "SERVICE_BOOKED",
    "title": "New service booking",
    "message": "A student booked your service 'Python tutoring'.",
    "data": {
      "booking_id": "booking-uuid",
      "service_id": "service-uuid",
      "student_id": "student-profile-uuid"
    },
    "is_read": false,
    "created_at": "2026-09-14T12:00:00+00:00"
  }
}

This is the same socket used for chat; do not create a second notification socket for the same user.

After opening the connection, send this text frame from Postman's WebSocket message composer:

{
  "type": "send_message",
  "payload": {
    "chat_room_id": "{{chat_room_id}}",
    "content": "Hello from Postman"
  }
}

Expected response event: new_message.

After opening the connection, send this text frame:

{
  "type": "fetch_history",
  "payload": {
    "chat_room_id": "{{chat_room_id}}",
    "before_message_id": null,
    "limit": 30
  }
}

Expected response event: history.

After opening the connection, send this text frame:

{
  "type": "mark_read",
  "payload": {
    "chat_room_id": "{{chat_room_id}}",
    "message_id": "{{message_id}}"
  }
}

Expected response event: read_receipt to other room members.

After opening the connection, send this text frame:

{
  "type": "typing",
  "payload": {
    "chat_room_id": "{{chat_room_id}}",
    "is_typing": true
  }
}

Expected response event: typing to other room members.
